26-                           which is determined based on whether stdout is a
27-                           terminal.
28:      --debugger           Launch the backend in a debugging console.
29-                           Currently only supported on LLVM backend.
30:      --debugger-batch     Launch the backend in a debugging console in batch
31-                           mode. Currently only supported on LLVM backend.
32:      --debugger-command FILE  Execute GDB commands from FILE to debug program.
33-                               Currently only supported on LLVM backend.
34-  -d, --definition DIR     Exact path to the kompiled directory.
35:      --depth N            Execute at most N rewrite steps
36-      --dry-run            Do not execute backend, but instead print the
37-                           command that would be executed to stdout.
38-      --execute-to-branch  Execute until a non-deterministic state is reached, then exit.
39:                           Requires the --enable-search option to have been passed to kompile
40-                           on the LLVM backend.
41-      --haskell-backend-command CMD  use CMD instead of kore-exec to invoke
--
45-                           stdin/stdout via cells with "stream" attribute.
46-                           Defaults to enabled when performing concrete
47:                           execution, and disabled when --search is passed.
48-      --no-expand-macros   Don't expand macros in initial configuration.
49-                           This assumes that the initial configuration contains
50-                           no macro terms. Behavior is undefined if this is not
51-                           true.
52:      --no-pattern         Skip pattern matching the result of searches on the
53:                           llvm backend against the default search pattern.
54-      --no-substitution-filtering  Don't filter conjuncts with anonymous
55-                                   variables from substitution output
--
67-                           `cat foo.kore` is invoked and the result on stdout
68-                           is used as the value of $PGM as a KORE term.
69:      --pattern PAT        Use PAT as the search pattern with --search. Can
70:                           also be used without --search to match the output
71-                           configuration against a pattern and print the
72-                           substitution. Not supported on LLVM backend.
--
74-                           Ignores `--output`.
75-      --save-temps         Do not delete temporary files when krun terminates.
76:      --search             Search for all possible output states after
77-                           rewriting. Only supported on symbolic backends.
78:      --search-all         Like --search, but also return interim states
79:      --search-final       Synonym for --search
80:      --search-one-or-more-steps  Like --search-all, but do not include the
